#: src/main.ui:435
msgid ""
"A desktop notification shows while Ubuntu Hello looks for your face, then "
"reports the result. Failed attempts stay in the notification list."
msgstr ""
"Hōʻike ʻia kahi leka hoʻomaopopo papa ʻoiai ʻo Ubuntu Hello e ʻimi ana i kou "
"helehelena, a laila hōʻike i ka hopena. Noho nā hoʻāʻo ʻole i ka papa inoa "
"hoʻolaha."

#: src/main.ui:466
msgid "Show notifications"
msgstr "Hōʻike i nā hoʻolaha"

#: src/main.ui:472
msgid ""
"One card per face-authentication attempt, updated in place with the result."
msgstr ""
"Hoʻokahi kāleka no ka hoʻāʻo ʻana i ka hōʻoia ʻana i ke alo, i hoʻonui ʻia "
"ma kahi me ka hopena."

#: src/main.ui:503
msgid "Notification sounds"
msgstr "Kani hoʻolaha"

#: src/main.ui:509
msgid "Play the system sound for a recognized or failed attempt."
msgstr ""
"E hoʻokani i ke kani ʻōnaehana no kahi hoʻāʻo ʻike ʻia a ʻaʻole i hāʻule."

#: src/main.ui:540
msgid "Include diagnostics"
msgstr "Hoʻokomo i nā diagnostics"

#: src/main.ui:546
msgid ""
"Add the model, certainty vs. threshold, frames, camera and timing to each "
"card. Useful when reporting a problem."
msgstr ""
"E hoʻohui i ke kumu hoʻohālike, ʻoiaʻiʻo a me ka paepae, nā kiʻi paʻi kiʻi, "
"ka pahupaʻikiʻi a me ka manawa i kēlā me kēia kāleka. Pono i ka hōʻike ʻana "
"i kahi pilikia."

#: src/main.ui:610 src/onboarding.ui:707
msgid "Keyring / KWallet Auto-Unlock"
msgstr "Hoʻopaʻa kī / KWallet Wehe-Aunoa"

#: src/main.ui:624
msgid ""
"Enable face authentication to automatically unlock your login keyring or "
"KWallet on login. This securely stores your password sealed in the TPM when "
"available, or encrypted with AES-256-GCM using a root-only master key. Face "
"auth sets PAM_AUTHTOK for pam_gnome_keyring or pam_kwallet5 depending on "
"your desktop."
msgstr ""
"E hoʻā i ka hōʻoia maka e wehe ʻakomi i kāu kī hoʻopaʻa inoa a i ʻole "
"KWallet ma ke komo ʻana. Mālama kēia i kāu ʻōlelo huna i hoʻopaʻa ʻia ma ka "
"TPM ke loaʻa, a i ʻole i hoʻopili ʻia me AES-256-GCM me ka hoʻohana ʻana i "
"kahi kī kumu kumu-wale nō. Hoʻonohonoho ʻia ke alo o ka mana PAM_AUTHTOK no "
"pam_gnome_keyring a i ʻole pam_kwallet5 ma muli o kāu pākaukau."

#: src/main.ui:652
msgid "Current Status:"
msgstr "Kūlana o kēia manawa:"

#: src/main.ui:661
msgid "Checking..."
msgstr "Ke nānā nei..."

#: src/main.ui:672
msgid "Enable Auto-Unlock"
msgstr "E ho'ā i ka wehe 'akomi"

#: src/main.ui:700
msgid "Keyring"
msgstr "Kiʻi kī"

#: src/main.ui:736
msgid "Display language"
msgstr "ʻŌlelo hōʻike"

#: src/main.ui:750
msgid "Automatic follows the system language. Changes apply immediately."
msgstr ""
"Hahai ka ʻŌlelo Aunoa i ka ʻōlelo ʻōnaehana. Hoʻopili koke ʻia nā loli."

#: src/main.ui:773 src/main.ui:792
msgid "Language"
msgstr "ʻŌlelo"

#: src/main.ui:813
msgid "Ubuntu Hello"
msgstr "Ubuntu Hello"

#: src/main.ui:823
msgid "Facial authentication for Linux"
msgstr "Hōʻoiaʻiʻo maka no Linux"

#: src/main.ui:832
msgid "Version unknown"
msgstr "ʻAʻole ʻike ʻia ka mana"

#: src/main.ui:846
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://github.com/ventura8/ubuntu-hello\">Open GitHub link</a> "
msgstr ""
"<a href=\"https://github.com/ventura8/ubuntu-hello\">Wehe i ka loulou "
"GitHub</a>"

#: src/main.ui:853
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://github.com/ventura8/Ubuntu-Hello/issues\">Report a problem "
"or suggest a feature</a>"
msgstr ""
"<a href=\"https://github.com/ventura8/Ubuntu-Hello/issues\">Hōʻike i kahi "
"pilikia a i ʻole e hōʻike i kahi hiʻohiʻona</a>"

#: src/main.ui:865
msgid "About"
msgstr "E pili ana"

#: src/onboarding.ui:9 src/onboarding.ui:14
msgid "Welcome to Ubuntu Hello"
msgstr "Welina mai iā Ubuntu Hello"

#: src/onboarding.ui:51
msgid "Setup is done!"
msgstr "Ua pau ka hoʻonohonoho ʻana!"

#: src/onboarding.ui:67
msgid ""
"We're done! Ubuntu Hello is now active on this computer. Try doing anything "
"you would normally have to type your password for to authenticate, like "
"running a command with sudo. If you enabled keyring auto-unlock, your login "
"keyring or KWallet will also be unlocked automatically on login.\n"
"\n"
"You can open the Ubuntu Hello Configurator later on to change more advanced "
"settings or add additional models. Press Finish below to close this window "
"and open the Ubuntu Hello Configurator. "
msgstr ""
"Ua pau mākou! Ubuntu Hello i kēia manawa ma kēia kamepiula. E hoʻāʻo e hana "
"i kekahi mea āu e pono ai e paʻi i kāu ʻōlelo huna no ka hōʻoia ʻana, e like "
"me ka holo ʻana i kahi kauoha me sudo. Inā hiki iā ʻoe ke hoʻā i ka wehe "
"ʻana i ke kī kī, e wehe ʻokoʻa ʻia kāu kī kī a i ʻole KWallet ma ke komo "
"ʻana.\n"
"\n"
"Hiki iā ʻoe ke wehe i ka Ubuntu Hello Configurator ma hope aku e hoʻololi i "
"nā hoʻonohonoho holomua a i ʻole e hoʻohui i nā hiʻohiʻona hou. E kaomi i ka "
"Finish ma lalo e pani i kēia puka aniani a wehe i ka Ubuntu Hello "
"Configurator."

#: src/onboarding.ui:103
msgid "Setting a certainty policy"
msgstr "Hoʻonohonoho i kahi kulekele paʻa"

#: src/onboarding.ui:119
msgid ""
"Because of changes in angles, distance, and other factors a face match is "
"never exactly the same as the stored face model. On this page you can set "
"how strict Ubuntu Hello should be."
msgstr ""
"Ma muli o ka hoʻololi ʻana i nā kihi, ka mamao, a me nā mea ʻē aʻe, ʻaʻole i "
"like ka hoʻohālikelike ʻana i ke alo me ke kumu hoʻohālike i mālama ʻia. Ma "
"kēia ʻaoʻao hiki iā ʻoe ke hoʻonohonoho i ke koʻikoʻi o Ubuntu Hello pono."

#: src/onboarding.ui:149
msgid "Fast"
msgstr "wikiwiki"

#: src/onboarding.ui:158
msgid ""
"Allows more fuzzy matches, \n"
"but speeds up the scanning process greatly."
msgstr ""
"Hāʻawi i nā pāʻani fuzzy hou aʻe, \n"
"akā, hoʻoikaika nui i ke kaʻina hana scan."

#: src/onboarding.ui:181
msgid "Balanced"
msgstr "Kaulike"

#: src/onboarding.ui:190
msgid ""
"Still relatively quick detection, \n"
"but might not log you in when further away."
msgstr ""
"ʻIke wikiwiki nō naʻe, \n"
"akā ʻaʻole paha e hoʻopaʻa inoa iā ʻoe i kahi mamao aku."

#: src/onboarding.ui:212
msgid "Secure"
msgstr "Paʻa"

#: src/onboarding.ui:222
msgid ""
"The slightly safer option, \n"
"but will take much longer to authenticate you"
msgstr ""
"ʻO ke koho palekana iki, \n"
"akā lōʻihi ka lōʻihi o ka hōʻoia ʻana iā ʻoe"

#: src/onboarding.ui:332
msgid "Skip for now"
msgstr "Holo i kēia manawa"

#: src/onboarding.ui:337
msgid ""
"You can add more face models later from Settings or with: sudo ubuntu-hello "
"add"
msgstr ""
"Hiki iā ʻoe ke hoʻohui i nā hiʻohiʻona helehelena hou aʻe ma hope mai "
"Settings a i ʻole: sudo ubuntu-hello add"

#: src/onboarding.ui:355 src/onboarding.ui:482
msgid "Configuring webcam"
msgstr "Ke hoʻonohonoho nei i ka webcam"

#: src/onboarding.ui:387
msgid "Is the infrared emitter flashing ?"
msgstr "Ke kukuna nei ka infrared emitter?"

#: src/onboarding.ui:399
msgid ""
"Look at the camera you selected: an infrared camera shows a small light that "
"blinks while Ubuntu Hello tests it. This tells us whether it can see your "
"face in the dark."
msgstr ""
"E nānā i ka pahupaʻikiʻi āu i koho ai: hōʻike ka pahupaʻikiʻi infrared i "
"kahi kukui liʻiliʻi e ʻā ana i ka wā e hoʻāʻo ai ʻo Ubuntu Hello iā ia. "
"Hōʻike kēia iā mākou inā hiki iā ia ke ʻike i kou helehelena i ka pōʻeleʻele."

#: src/onboarding.ui:433
msgid "Yes, it flashes"
msgstr "ʻAe, ʻālohilohi"

#: src/onboarding.ui:459
msgid "No, nothing flashes"
msgstr "ʻAʻole, ʻaʻohe mea uila"

#: src/onboarding.ui:498
msgid ""
"Ubuntu Hello will search your system automatically for any available "
"cameras, so make sure your webcam is connected. After detection a list of "
"usable webcams will be shown. Pick the one you want to use and click Next."
msgstr ""
"Ubuntu Hello e ʻimi maʻalahi i kāu ʻōnaehana no nā pahupaʻikiʻi i loaʻa, no "
"laila e hoʻopaʻa pono i ka pili ʻana o kāu webcam. Ma hope o ka ʻike ʻana e "
"hōʻike ʻia kahi papa inoa o nā webcams hoʻohana. E koho i ka mea āu e "
"makemake ai e hoʻohana a kaomi Next."

#: src/onboarding.ui:517
msgid "Testing your webcams, please wait..."
msgstr "Ke hoʻāʻo nei i kāu webcams, e ʻoluʻolu e kali..."

#: src/onboarding.ui:563
msgid "Downloading data files"
msgstr "Hoʻoiho ʻana i nā faila ʻikepili"

#: src/onboarding.ui:579
msgid ""
"Ubuntu Hello needs three pre trained facial recognition datasets to be able "
"to recognise you, which will be downloaded now. You can see the download "
"progress below."
msgstr ""
"Pono ʻo Ubuntu Hello i ʻekolu mau ʻikepili ʻike maka i hoʻomaʻamaʻa mua ʻia "
"i hiki ke ʻike iā ʻoe, e hoʻoiho ʻia i kēia manawa. Hiki iā ʻoe ke ʻike i ka "
"holomua download ma lalo nei."

#: src/onboarding.ui:603
msgid "Starting download..."
msgstr "Ke hoʻomaka nei e hoʻoiho..."

#: src/onboarding.ui:646
msgid "Welcome to Ubuntu Hello!"
msgstr "Welina mai iā Ubuntu Hello!"

#: src/onboarding.ui:658
msgid "Version"
msgstr "Manao"

#: src/onboarding.ui:672
msgid ""
"This wizard will walk you through the setup process and automatically "
"configure Ubuntu Hello for you. Press next to continue."
msgstr ""
"Na kēia wizard e alakaʻi iā ʻoe ma ke kaʻina hana hoʻonohonoho a "
"hoʻonohonoho aunoa iā Ubuntu Hello nou. E kaomi aʻe e hoʻomau."

#: src/onboarding.ui:723
msgid ""
"Ubuntu Hello can automatically unlock your login keyring or KWallet using "
"face authentication, preventing password prompts after logging in."
msgstr ""
"Hiki iā Ubuntu Hello ke wehe ʻokoʻa i kāu kī hoʻopaʻa inoa a i ʻole KWallet "
"me ka hoʻohana ʻana i ka hōʻoia maka, e pale ana i ka ʻōlelo huna ma hope o "
"ke komo ʻana."

#: src/onboarding.ui:735
msgid "Enable automatic keyring/KWallet unlocking"
msgstr "E hoʻā i ke kī ʻakomi/KWallet wehe"

#: src/onboarding.ui:763
msgid "Confirm password"
msgstr "Hōʻoia i ka ʻŌlelo Huna"

#: src/onboarding.ui:820
msgid "Back"
msgstr "Ke kua"

#: src/onboarding.ui:855
msgid "Finish setup"
msgstr "Hoʻopau i ka hoʻonohonoho"

#: src/onboarding.ui:882
msgid "Next"
msgstr "Aʻe"

